You ought not to leave your citadels unguarded (except maybe Dol Amroth).
Y6 Press 'Return' when you've finished reading: 
The Map:
On the map are various signs. They are:
":" = Rough Terrain.
"." = Grass.
"T" = Trees.
"&" = Swamp. Can only be passed when Gollum is with you and untied.
"M" = Mountain.
""" = River. Cannot be crossed unless at Ford or Road.
"-" = Road.
"=" = Main Road.
"+" = Ford.
"I" = Tower.
"D" = Mt. Doom. The Goal of the expedition.
"B" = Barad Dur. The Black Tower. The Citadel of Sauron.
Y6 Press 'Return' when you've finished reading: 
To the right of the terrain symbols are signs of monsters etc.
"o" = Orcs. 1-12 in each group.
"w" = Wolves. 1-12 in each group.
"b" = Balrog. There are 4 of them romping about.
"n" = Nazgul. There are 9 of these. If you get to Mt. Doom all surviving
Nazgul will attack you!
"h" = Haradrim. 1-12 in each bunch.
"t" = Trolls. 1-12 in each party.
"g" = Gollum. He is, thank God, unique.
"F" = The Fellowship.
"?" = A traitor?
Y6 Press 'Return' when you've finished reading: 
There are also some useful commands:
ON           Take on the Ring: increases strength and sight with 2.
             If worn too long the bearer can become a semi-ringwraith,
             then he will dissappear and start heading for the Black Tower
             and you will have to find and slay him!
OFF          Remove the Ring from the bearers finger. Might not work!
FOLLOW-ROAD  Follow a Road or Main Road north, that is upwards.
KILL         If you have caught Gollum and not wont him, then kill him.
ASK          Ask Gollum of the Way. Note! He will lead you to Shelob
             and she is Strong, so you might get killed.
0            Do nothing more this turn.
THROW        If you reach Mt. Doom with the Ring off and throw it you have won!
HELP         Gives you short instructions.
REPORT       Gives you the current status of the fellowship!
TIE          Tie Gollum. When tied, Gollum refuses to answer your questions,
             and will not lead you through swamps, but he cannot seize the
             Ring.
UNTIE        Untie Gollum. Will make it possible for you to cross swamps.
             He will also answer your questions when he has recovered from
             being tied. He may, however, attempt to seize the Ring at any
             time!
MAP          Draws the Scanner.
QUIT-GAME    Exactly what it says.
Y6 Press 'Return' when you've finished reading: 
How to move:
You type in your direction and how far you want to go. e.g.
NW    N   NE
    . ! .         NE2 Moves you up to 2 steps NE
 W  - + -  E      If you want to go as far as possible type a "+"
    . ! .         e.g. E+ moves you as far as possible eastwards.
SW    S   SE
 
If you run into an enemy there will be a fight until all of you or the
enemies have died or the enemies have fled.
 
If you have less than 2 Movement Points (MPs) left at the end of movement
you will get tired.
Y6 Press 'Return' when you've finished reading: 
How to fight:
When you run into a monster you will have the choises of attacking Together
or Individually. If the Monsters attack you, they chose the option.
 
As a result of the fight-round one of you may get Killed, Unconscious, or
Captured, the monsters may get Killed or they may flee.
If all monsters are killed, the captives will be freed, and all
unconscious members will regain consciousness.
Y6 Press 'Return' when you've finished reading: 
If the Ringbearer becomes a Ringwraith he will dissappear from the company and
start moving towards Barad Dur. If he reaches that place of evil, you have lost
the game, (and your lives). The traitor will appear on your map as a
Questionmark, "?". If you reach the traitor, there is a possibility that you
will kill him and regain the Ring. There is also the possibility that he will
kill the lot of you!
 
Also if any member of the Fellowship seizes the Ring, he will start
moving towards Minas Tirith, (The South), till he becomes a Ringwraith. If that
occurs, he will move towards Barad Dur.
 
 
